    symptoms: 'You have to slam or lift the door to latch it, it pops back open, or it rattles when closed.',
    quickCheck: ['With the door open, turn the knob: does the latch move freely in and out? If not, the lockset is the problem, not the strike.', 'Rub lipstick, dry-erase marker or crayon on the latch tongue, close the door, and see where it marks the strike plate — above, below, or in front of the opening.', 'Tighten the hinges first; a sagging door is the usual reason the latch drops below the strike.'],
